--TEST--
A `Core\Task::all` field typed bare `callable` whose function takes a parameter throws a `LogicError` before any field runs — `rule:concurrency/all-answers-a-typed-shape`
--FILE--
<?nvs
type Page = {user: mixed, orders: mixed};

callable $user = fn(int $id): int => $id;
callable $orders = fn(): int => 3;
try {
    Page $page = Core\Task::all({user: $user, orders: $orders});
    echo "not reached\n";
} catch (LogicError $e) {
    echo $e->message, "\n";
}
--EXPECT--
Core\Task::all calls each field's function with no arguments, and one of them has 1 parameter(s)
